                <pb facs="0184" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg76"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-29"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received November 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson reports that the attack of the insurgents on Nictheroy and Santa
                    Catharina has been repulsed, the <hi rendition="#italic">Pallas</hi> being
                    wrecked and the <hi rendition="#italic">Madeira</hi> burned. He says that the
                    situation appears favorable to the Government.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
